Handle the 0xFFFF "no interrupt pending" value returned by the MSM VIC.

When the kernel is entered from HaRET (i.e. from within Windows Mobile) rather
than from cLK/MAGLDR, VIC_IRQ_VEC_PEND_RD returns 0x0000FFFF instead of
0xFFFFFFFF when no interrupt is pending. The existing check only tests for
0xFFFFFFFF, so the value is taken for a valid interrupt number and the kernel
drowns in "Bad IRQ65535" from handle_IRQ(), never making progress.

The working 2.6.32 HD2 kernels (tytung/android_kernel_htcleo-2.6.32) carry the
same three instructions; they were never forwarded to the 3.0 qsd8k-legacy tree
because that tree is only ever booted through cLK.

--- a/arch/arm/mach-msm/include/mach/entry-macro-vic.S
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-msm/include/mach/entry-macro-vic.S
@@ -34,4 +34,7 @@
 	ldr	\irqnr, [\base, #0xD0]
 	ldr	\irqnr, [\base, #0xD4]
 	cmp	\irqnr, #0xffffffff
+	movne	\tmp, #0xff
+	orrne	\tmp, #0xff00
+	cmpne	\irqnr, \tmp
 	.endm
